      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "This is an issue with the shader that's being used.\nDepth of Field unfortunately requires that things actually write to the Depth texture in order to properly blur them. \"Unlit/Texture\" does not do this.\nShaders that don't write to the depth texture properly will be blurred as if they are at an infinite distance away. There is no fix for this other than fixing the shader, or using a different shader.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-10-19T23:32:00.885Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I noticed that today and I really dislike this.\nI have a public world with some avatars on it and I wanted to take some photos for new avatar thumbnails.\nBUT This is the result of that (attached file).\nThe eyes are very weirdly blurry and the inside of my mouth too.\nFor the Eyes they have the shader \"Unlit/Texture\".\nI kinda could fix it if I don't use that (I tested it with an older poiyomi version that was still in the project) but my mouth was really blurry if I talk if the focus kicks in on me. It's unusable for me at that point. \nI use btw. for all my avatars that are a little bit older poiyomi shader v6.1.\nAnd if I have this problem with my eyes and mouth and the focus is set to the background, my eyes and mouth are sharp and the rest of me blurry. so....something is really wrong.",
